-- Migration 198: Terms of Service content — corrective apply (contact email aligned)
--
-- COURTZON_MIGRATION_ENV: PRODUCTION_SAFE
--
-- PURPOSE
--   Migration 197 carried an exact old/new content guard. On production the
--   live Terms text had previously been edited through the CMS (section 9
--   contact: mniazyy@gmail.com instead of the seed's legal@courtzon.com), so
--   197 matched neither value and affected 0 rows there. This migration
--   applies the final restructured document (12 sections incl. 7.
--   Cancellations & Refunds, contact mniazyy@gmail.com) using a guard that is
--   immune to old-content drift: update unless the row ALREADY holds the final
--   content, and only when it still looks like the original Terms document
--   (fingerprint), so a heavily rewritten CMS document is never clobbered.
--
-- SAFETY / IDEMPOTENCY
--   * Data-only UPDATE of cms_section_blocks (no schema change).
--   * Re-runs are no-ops: content <> final fails once the row is final.
--   * Admin rewrites that no longer contain the Terms fingerprint are skipped.
--   * Fresh environments already receive the final content from
--     database/seeds/001_baseline.sql (entrypoint stamps, does not run).
--   * Feeds both /terms and the registration consent modal (same CMS page).

-- ── 1. Main Terms of Service body (text block) ───────────────────────────────

UPDATE `cms_section_blocks`
SET `content` = '{"html":"<h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3><p>By using CourtZon, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use our platform.</p><h3>2. Account Registration</h3><p>You must provide accurate information when creating an account. You are responsible for all activities under your account.</p><h3>3. CourtZon Platform &amp; Third-Party Providers</h3><p>CourtZon is a technology platform that connects users with independent facilities, clubs, academies, event organizers, sellers, and other service providers.</p><p>Unless expressly stated otherwise, CourtZon is not the provider of the third-party products or services made available through the platform. The payment of an amount through the CourtZon platform does not, by itself, make CourtZon the provider, seller, owner, or operator of the underlying product or service.</p><p>The following are provided by independent third parties, not by CourtZon:</p><ul><li>Court bookings, clubs, and sports facilities</li><li>Academies and services offered by facilities or clubs</li><li>Events and services offered by their respective organizers</li><li>Marketplace products sold by independent sellers</li></ul><p>CourtZon directly provides subscription services only to sellers, organizations, clubs, facilities, and other business users that subscribe to CourtZon.</p><h3>4. Bookings, Facilities &amp; Services</h3><ul><li>Court bookings are provided by the relevant facility, club, or service provider. Facilities and clubs are independent entities from CourtZon.</li><li>Academies and other services are provided by their respective providers, and events are provided by their respective organizers.</li><li>Cancellation, rescheduling, refund, and other service conditions may be determined by the relevant provider and are presented to the user during the relevant transaction where supported.</li></ul><p>CourtZon does not guarantee the quality, availability, or performance of third-party services, except where expressly stated otherwise.</p><h3>5. Marketplace &amp; Sellers</h3><ul><li>Marketplace products are offered by independent sellers.</li><li>Sellers are responsible for their products and their applicable seller policies.</li><li>Returns, cancellations, exchanges, and refunds are subject to the applicable seller and product conditions presented to the user.</li><li>CourtZon does not own or manufacture Marketplace products unless explicitly stated otherwise.</li></ul><h3>6. Payments</h3><p>Payments for transactions made through the platform are processed securely through CourtZon payment providers. CourtZon may facilitate or process payments on the platform, but payment processing does not make CourtZon the provider, seller, owner, or operator of the underlying third-party service or product.</p><h3>7. Cancellations &amp; Refunds</h3><p>The applicable policy depends on what was purchased and who provides it:</p><ul><li><strong>Third-party bookings, facilities, academies, and events</strong> &mdash; see section 7.1.</li><li><strong>Marketplace products</strong> &mdash; see section 7.2.</li><li><strong>CourtZon subscriptions</strong> &mdash; see section 7.3.</li></ul><h4>7.1 Third-Party Bookings &amp; Services</h4><p>Bookings and services made through CourtZon are provided by the relevant facility, club, academy, event organizer, or other service provider.</p><p>Any cancellation, rescheduling, refund, or other booking conditions are subject to the policies and terms established by the relevant service provider and displayed to the user during the booking process.</p><p>CourtZon does not independently determine refund eligibility for third-party bookings unless expressly stated otherwise.</p><h4>7.2 Marketplace Purchases</h4><p>Products available through the CourtZon Marketplace are offered by independent sellers.</p><p>Returns, cancellations, refunds, exchanges, and other product-related matters are subject to the applicable seller and product policies presented to the user at or before the time of purchase.</p><p>CourtZon does not own or manufacture Marketplace products unless expressly stated otherwise.</p><h4>7.3 CourtZon Subscriptions</h4><p>Subscriptions purchased directly from CourtZon by sellers, organizations, clubs, facilities, or other business users are services provided by CourtZon.</p><p>Cancellation and refund eligibility for these subscriptions will be determined according to the applicable subscription plan, subscription agreement, billing terms, and any refund conditions communicated by CourtZon.</p><p>Unless otherwise expressly stated, cancelling a subscription does not automatically entitle the subscriber to a refund for amounts already paid or for the remaining portion of an active subscription period.</p><p>Where a refund is approved by CourtZon, it will normally be processed through the original payment method, subject to the applicable payment provider&rsquo;s processing procedures.</p><h4>7.4 Payment Errors</h4><p>If a user believes they have been charged incorrectly, charged more than once, or charged for a transaction that was not successfully completed, the user should contact CourtZon with the relevant transaction or booking information.</p><p>CourtZon will review the transaction records and, where an error attributable to CourtZon or its payment processing is confirmed, take the appropriate corrective action.</p><h4>7.5 Refund Processing</h4><p>Where a refund is approved, the time required for the refunded amount to appear in the user&rsquo;s account may depend on the payment provider, bank, card issuer, or other financial institution.</p><p>CourtZon is not responsible for delays caused by third-party payment providers or financial institutions.</p><h3>8. User Conduct</h3><p>You agree not to misuse our platform, violate laws, harass other users, or submit false information.</p><h3>9. Intellectual Property</h3><p>All content and trademarks on CourtZon are owned by or licensed to us. Do not copy or modify without permission.</p><h3>10. Limitation of Liability</h3><p>CourtZon is provided as is. We are not liable for indirect or consequential damages.</p><h3>11. Changes to These Terms</h3><p>We may update these terms. Continued use constitutes acceptance.</p><h3>12. Contact Us</h3><p>For questions: mniazyy@gmail.com.</p>"}'
WHERE `block_key` = 'term_text'
  AND `block_type` = 'text'
  AND `page_id` = (SELECT `id` FROM `cms_pages` WHERE `slug` = 'terms')
  AND `content` <> '{"html":"<h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3><p>By using CourtZon, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use our platform.</p><h3>2. Account Registration</h3><p>You must provide accurate information when creating an account. You are responsible for all activities under your account.</p><h3>3. CourtZon Platform &amp; Third-Party Providers</h3><p>CourtZon is a technology platform that connects users with independent facilities, clubs, academies, event organizers, sellers, and other service providers.</p><p>Unless expressly stated otherwise, CourtZon is not the provider of the third-party products or services made available through the platform. The payment of an amount through the CourtZon platform does not, by itself, make CourtZon the provider, seller, owner, or operator of the underlying product or service.</p><p>The following are provided by independent third parties, not by CourtZon:</p><ul><li>Court bookings, clubs, and sports facilities</li><li>Academies and services offered by facilities or clubs</li><li>Events and services offered by their respective organizers</li><li>Marketplace products sold by independent sellers</li></ul><p>CourtZon directly provides subscription services only to sellers, organizations, clubs, facilities, and other business users that subscribe to CourtZon.</p><h3>4. Bookings, Facilities &amp; Services</h3><ul><li>Court bookings are provided by the relevant facility, club, or service provider. Facilities and clubs are independent entities from CourtZon.</li><li>Academies and other services are provided by their respective providers, and events are provided by their respective organizers.</li><li>Cancellation, rescheduling, refund, and other service conditions may be determined by the relevant provider and are presented to the user during the relevant transaction where supported.</li></ul><p>CourtZon does not guarantee the quality, availability, or performance of third-party services, except where expressly stated otherwise.</p><h3>5. Marketplace &amp; Sellers</h3><ul><li>Marketplace products are offered by independent sellers.</li><li>Sellers are responsible for their products and their applicable seller policies.</li><li>Returns, cancellations, exchanges, and refunds are subject to the applicable seller and product conditions presented to the user.</li><li>CourtZon does not own or manufacture Marketplace products unless explicitly stated otherwise.</li></ul><h3>6. Payments</h3><p>Payments for transactions made through the platform are processed securely through CourtZon payment providers. CourtZon may facilitate or process payments on the platform, but payment processing does not make CourtZon the provider, seller, owner, or operator of the underlying third-party service or product.</p><h3>7. Cancellations &amp; Refunds</h3><p>The applicable policy depends on what was purchased and who provides it:</p><ul><li><strong>Third-party bookings, facilities, academies, and events</strong> &mdash; see section 7.1.</li><li><strong>Marketplace products</strong> &mdash; see section 7.2.</li><li><strong>CourtZon subscriptions</strong> &mdash; see section 7.3.</li></ul><h4>7.1 Third-Party Bookings &amp; Services</h4><p>Bookings and services made through CourtZon are provided by the relevant facility, club, academy, event organizer, or other service provider.</p><p>Any cancellation, rescheduling, refund, or other booking conditions are subject to the policies and terms established by the relevant service provider and displayed to the user during the booking process.</p><p>CourtZon does not independently determine refund eligibility for third-party bookings unless expressly stated otherwise.</p><h4>7.2 Marketplace Purchases</h4><p>Products available through the CourtZon Marketplace are offered by independent sellers.</p><p>Returns, cancellations, refunds, exchanges, and other product-related matters are subject to the applicable seller and product policies presented to the user at or before the time of purchase.</p><p>CourtZon does not own or manufacture Marketplace products unless expressly stated otherwise.</p><h4>7.3 CourtZon Subscriptions</h4><p>Subscriptions purchased directly from CourtZon by sellers, organizations, clubs, facilities, or other business users are services provided by CourtZon.</p><p>Cancellation and refund eligibility for these subscriptions will be determined according to the applicable subscription plan, subscription agreement, billing terms, and any refund conditions communicated by CourtZon.</p><p>Unless otherwise expressly stated, cancelling a subscription does not automatically entitle the subscriber to a refund for amounts already paid or for the remaining portion of an active subscription period.</p><p>Where a refund is approved by CourtZon, it will normally be processed through the original payment method, subject to the applicable payment provider&rsquo;s processing procedures.</p><h4>7.4 Payment Errors</h4><p>If a user believes they have been charged incorrectly, charged more than once, or charged for a transaction that was not successfully completed, the user should contact CourtZon with the relevant transaction or booking information.</p><p>CourtZon will review the transaction records and, where an error attributable to CourtZon or its payment processing is confirmed, take the appropriate corrective action.</p><h4>7.5 Refund Processing</h4><p>Where a refund is approved, the time required for the refunded amount to appear in the user&rsquo;s account may depend on the payment provider, bank, card issuer, or other financial institution.</p><p>CourtZon is not responsible for delays caused by third-party payment providers or financial institutions.</p><h3>8. User Conduct</h3><p>You agree not to misuse our platform, violate laws, harass other users, or submit false information.</p><h3>9. Intellectual Property</h3><p>All content and trademarks on CourtZon are owned by or licensed to us. Do not copy or modify without permission.</p><h3>10. Limitation of Liability</h3><p>CourtZon is provided as is. We are not liable for indirect or consequential damages.</p><h3>11. Changes to These Terms</h3><p>We may update these terms. Continued use constitutes acceptance.</p><h3>12. Contact Us</h3><p>For questions: mniazyy@gmail.com.</p>"}'
  AND `content` LIKE '%<h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>%';

-- ── 2. Hero "Last updated" subheading ────────────────────────────────────────

UPDATE `cms_section_blocks`
SET `content` = '{"heading":"Terms of Service","subheading":"Last updated: October 2026"}'
WHERE `block_key` = 'term_hero'
  AND `block_type` = 'hero'
  AND `page_id` = (SELECT `id` FROM `cms_pages` WHERE `slug` = 'terms')
  AND `content` <> '{"heading":"Terms of Service","subheading":"Last updated: October 2026"}'
  AND `content` LIKE '%Terms of Service%';
